@page "/{culture}/legal/privacy"
@inherits PageCore<PrivacyPage>

<HeadComponent Title="@Translations.Module.Legal.PrivacyPolicy" Url=@($"/{Culture}/legal/privacy") Index="false"></HeadComponent>

<div class="support-container">
    @if (Language == AppLanguage.pt)
    {
        <h1 class="support-title">Política de Privacidade</h1>
        <div class="support-subtitle">
            Sua privacidade é uma prioridade no <b>@AppInfo.Title</b> (<a href="@AppInfo.WebSite" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@AppInfo.WebSite</a>), operado pela DRMA Tech (Delivering Reliable Modern Apps Tech OÜ).<br />
            Por favor, leia esta política com atenção para entender como tratamos seus dados.
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>1. Dados coletados</h2>
            <p>Coletamos e armazenamos informações como: endereço de e-mail, data de login e endereço IP, país de acesso (via IP) e configurações básicas do usuário. O login é opcional, mas alguns recursos estão disponíveis apenas para usuários autenticados. Dados técnicos e de navegação também podem ser coletados mesmo sem autenticação.</p>
            <p>Todas as informações sobre filmes e séries são obtidas de serviços externos como TMDb, IMDb, JustWatch, entre outros. A plataforma apenas organiza, apresenta e personaliza esse conteúdo.</p>
            <p>Não coletamos dados pessoais sensíveis ou geolocalização precisa sem consentimento explícito.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>2. Cookies e tecnologias similares</h2>
            <p>Utilizamos cookies próprios e armazenamento de sessão para manter preferências do usuário, autenticação e funcionalidades da plataforma. Também utilizamos cookies de terceiros de serviços como Google AdSense para exibir anúncios personalizados com base em sua atividade e preferências.</p>
            <p><b>Importante:</b> Devido à estrutura AppTrackingTransparency (ATT) da Apple, que exige permissão explícita do usuário para rastreamento entre aplicativos e sites, as tecnologias de rastreamento comportamental não estão operacionais em dispositivos Apple em nosso aplicativo. Não usamos nem instalamos estruturas de rastreamento que exijam o consentimento da ATT. Como resultado, a coleta de dados comportamentais e as análises relacionadas são limitadas ou indisponíveis em dispositivos Apple.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>3. Ferramentas de análise</h2>
            <p>Para melhorar a plataforma e entender os padrões de uso, utilizamos ferramentas como Google Analytics e Microsoft Clarity. Esses serviços podem coletar dados não identificáveis, como endereço IP, localização aproximada, tipo de navegador, duração da sessão e páginas visitadas.</p>
            <p><b>Observação:</b> Em dispositivos Apple, devido às restrições da ATT, o rastreamento comportamental e a coleta de dados entre aplicativos são limitados. Cumprimos integralmente essas restrições e não as ignoramos, portanto, os dados de usuários da Apple podem ser menos abrangentes ou ausentes.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>4. Compartilhamento de dados</h2>
            <p>Não compartilhamos seus dados pessoais com terceiros, exceto com parceiros técnicos essenciais para o funcionamento do serviço, incluindo provedores de login social, infraestrutura de hospedagem, análises e publicidade. Esses parceiros atuam sob rigorosos acordos de confidencialidade e controle de acesso.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>5. Armazenamento</h2>
            <p>Seus dados são armazenados em servidores da Microsoft Azure localizados nos Estados Unidos e podem ser replicados em outras regiões para garantir estabilidade e disponibilidade. Os dados são protegidos por práticas modernas de segurança, incluindo transmissão criptografada e controle de acesso.</p>
            <p>Quando uma conta é excluída, os dados pessoais são removidos do banco de dados principal. No entanto, certas informações podem ser retidas em sistemas isolados por até 6 meses por razões legais ou operacionais, como prevenção de fraudes, conformidade ou solicitações de investigação. Após esse período, os dados são permanentemente excluídos ou anonimizados.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>6. Direitos do usuário</h2>
            <p>Os usuários podem excluir suas contas a qualquer momento e solicitar a remoção de seus dados associados. Também é possível acessar ou modificar suas informações de conta usando as ferramentas disponíveis nas configurações do perfil. Se desejar obter uma cópia dos seus dados armazenados, entre em contato pelo canal de suporte.</p>
            <p>Se você tiver dúvidas sobre seus dados ou desejar exercer seus direitos sob as leis de privacidade aplicáveis ​​(GDPR, LGPD, CCPA/CPRA), entre em contato conosco por meio da página de suporte da plataforma.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>7. Listas públicas e privadas</h2>
            <p>A plataforma oferece listas públicas curadas que podem ser acessadas e compartilhadas por qualquer visitante. Usuários autenticados podem criar listas privadas com número limitado de itens. Essas listas permanecem privadas, mas podem ser compartilhadas por link público, a critério do usuário. Usuários pagos têm acesso a maior capacidade de listas.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>8. Crianças e menores de idade</h2>
            <p>A plataforma é destinada ao público geral e não coleta intencionalmente dados de menores de idade. Se tomarmos conhecimento do uso não autorizado de nossos serviços por crianças abaixo da idade permitida, os dados associados serão removidos mediante solicitação.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>9. Conformidade legal</h2>
            <p>Esta política de privacidade está alinhada com as regulamentações de privacidade e proteção de dados aplicáveis, incluindo GDPR, LGPD e leis equivalentes nas regiões onde operamos.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>10. Contato</h2>
            <p>Se tiver dúvidas, solicitações ou reclamações relacionadas aos seus dados pessoais, utilize a página de suporte disponível na plataforma.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>11. Atualizações</h2>
            <p>Esta política pode ser atualizada periodicamente para refletir mudanças na funcionalidade, nos serviços ou nas regulamentações aplicáveis. Recomendamos revisá-la ocasionalmente para se manter informado.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-footer">
            <p>Última atualização: 5 de agosto de 2025</p>
            <p>Ao utilizar este site, você concorda com esta Política de Privacidade e com os <a href=@($"/{Culture}/legal/terms")>Termos de Uso</a>.</p>
        </div>
    }
    else if (Language == AppLanguage.es)
    {
        <h1 class="support-title">Política de Privacidad</h1>
        <div class="support-subtitle">
            Tu privacidad es una prioridad en <b>@AppInfo.Title</b> (<a href="@AppInfo.WebSite" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@AppInfo.WebSite</a>), operado por DRMA Tech (Delivering Reliable Modern Apps Tech OÜ).<br />
            Por favor, lee esta política con atención para entender cómo manejamos tus datos.
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>1. Datos recopilados</h2>
            <p>Recopilamos y almacenamos información como: dirección de correo electrónico, fecha de inicio de sesión y dirección IP, país de acceso (a través de IP) y configuraciones básicas del usuario. El inicio de sesión es opcional, pero algunas funciones solo están disponibles para usuarios autenticados. También se pueden recopilar datos técnicos y de navegación incluso sin autenticación.</p>
            <p>Toda la información sobre películas y series proviene de servicios externos como TMDb, IMDb, JustWatch, entre otros. La plataforma solo organiza, presenta y personaliza este contenido.</p>
            <p>No recopilamos datos personales sensibles ni geolocalización precisa sin consentimiento explícito.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>2. Cookies y tecnologías similares</h2>
            <p>Utilizamos cookies propias y almacenamiento de sesión para mantener las preferencias del usuario, la autenticación y el funcionamiento de la plataforma. También usamos cookies de terceros de servicios como Google AdSense para mostrar anuncios personalizados según tu actividad y preferencias.</p>
            <p><b>Importante:</b> Debido al marco AppTrackingTransparency (ATT) de Apple, que requiere el permiso explícito del usuario para el seguimiento entre aplicaciones y sitios web, las tecnologías de seguimiento del comportamiento no están disponibles en los dispositivos Apple de nuestra aplicación. No utilizamos ni instalamos marcos de seguimiento que requieran el consentimiento de ATT. Por lo tanto, la recopilación de datos de comportamiento y los análisis relacionados son limitados o no están disponibles en los dispositivos Apple.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>3. Herramientas de análisis</h2>
            <p>Para mejorar la plataforma y comprender los patrones de uso, utilizamos herramientas como Google Analytics y Microsoft Clarity. Estos servicios pueden recopilar datos no identificables como dirección IP, ubicación aproximada, tipo de navegador, duración de la sesión y páginas visitadas.</p>
            <p><b>Nota:</b> En los dispositivos Apple, debido a las restricciones de ATT, el seguimiento del comportamiento y la recopilación de datos entre aplicaciones son limitados. Cumplimos plenamente con estas restricciones y no las eludimos, por lo que los datos de los usuarios de Apple podrían ser menos completos o inexistentes.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>4. Compartición de datos</h2>
            <p>No compartimos tus datos personales con terceros, salvo con socios técnicos esenciales para el funcionamiento básico, incluidos proveedores de inicio de sesión social, infraestructura de alojamiento, análisis y servicios de publicidad. Estos socios operan bajo estrictos controles de confidencialidad y acceso.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>5. Almacenamiento</h2>
            <p>Tus datos se almacenan en servidores de Microsoft Azure ubicados en los Estados Unidos y pueden replicarse en otras regiones para garantizar la estabilidad y disponibilidad. Los datos están protegidos mediante prácticas modernas de seguridad, como transmisión cifrada y acceso controlado.</p>
            <p>Cuando se elimina una cuenta, los datos personales se eliminan de la base de datos principal. Sin embargo, cierta información puede conservarse en sistemas aislados por hasta 6 meses por razones legales u operativas, como prevención de fraudes, cumplimiento o solicitudes de investigación. Después de este período, los datos se eliminan permanentemente o se anonimizan.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>6. Derechos del usuario</h2>
            <p>Los usuarios pueden eliminar sus cuentas en cualquier momento y solicitar la eliminación de sus datos asociados. También puedes acceder o modificar tu información de cuenta usando las herramientas disponibles en la configuración de perfil. Si deseas obtener una copia de tus datos almacenados, puedes contactarnos a través del canal de soporte.</p>
            <p>Si tiene preguntas sobre sus datos o desea ejercer sus derechos bajo las leyes de privacidad aplicables (GDPR, LGPD, CCPA/CPRA), contáctenos a través de la página de soporte de la plataforma.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>7. Listas públicas y privadas</h2>
            <p>La plataforma ofrece listas públicas curadas que pueden ser accedidas y compartidas por cualquier visitante. Los usuarios autenticados pueden crear listas privadas con un número limitado de elementos. Estas listas permanecen privadas, pero pueden compartirse mediante un enlace público, a discreción del usuario. Los usuarios pagos tienen acceso a una mayor capacidad de listas.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>8. Niños y menores de edad</h2>
            <p>La plataforma está destinada al público general y no recopila intencionadamente datos de menores de edad. Si llegamos a saber del uso no autorizado de nuestros servicios por parte de niños que no cumplan con la edad mínima permitida, eliminaremos los datos asociados tras recibir una solicitud.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>9. Cumplimiento legal</h2>
            <p>Esta política de privacidad está alineada con las normativas aplicables de privacidad y protección de datos, incluyendo el GDPR, la LGPD y leyes equivalentes en las regiones donde operamos.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>10. Contacto</h2>
            <p>Si tienes preguntas, solicitudes o reclamos relacionados con tus datos personales, utiliza la página de soporte disponible en la plataforma.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>11. Actualizaciones</h2>
            <p>Esta política puede actualizarse periódicamente para reflejar cambios en la funcionalidad, servicios o regulaciones aplicables. Recomendamos revisarla de vez en cuando para mantenerte informado.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-footer">
            <p>Última actualización: 5 de agosto de 2025</p>
            <p>Al utilizar este sitio, aceptas esta Política de Privacidad y los <a href=@($"/{Culture}/legal/terms")>Términos de Uso</a>.</p>
        </div>
    }
    else if (Language == AppLanguage.zh)
    {
        <h1 class="support-title">隐私政策</h1>
        <div class="support-subtitle">
            您的隐私是 <b>@AppInfo.Title</b> (<a href="@AppInfo.WebSite" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@AppInfo.WebSite</a>) 的首要任务，本平台由 DRMA Tech（Delivering Reliable Modern Apps Tech OÜ）运营。<br />
            请仔细阅读本政策，以了解我们如何处理您的数据。
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>1. 收集的数据</h2>
            <p>我们会收集和存储以下信息：电子邮箱地址、登录日期和 IP 地址、访问国家（通过 IP）、设备类型、浏览器类型和基本用户设置。登录为可选操作，但部分功能仅对已验证用户开放。即使未登录，技术和浏览数据也可能被收集。</p>
            <p>所有电影和电视剧信息均来自外部服务，如 TMDb、IMDb、JustWatch 等。平台仅对这些内容进行整理、组织并以个性化的方式展示。</p>
            <p>未经明确同意，我们不会收集敏感的个人数据或精确的地理位置。</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>2. Cookies 和类似技术</h2>
            <p>我们使用第一方 Cookie 和会话存储来维护用户偏好、身份验证和平台功能。第三方分析提供商可能会使用 Cookie 来分析使用模式。您可以通过浏览器或平台设置来管理或撤销同意。</p>
            <p><b>重要提示：</b>由于 Apple 的 AppTrackingTransparency (ATT) 框架要求用户明确许可才能进行跨应用和跨网站跟踪，因此我们的应用在 Apple 设备上不启用行为跟踪技术。我们不会使用或安装需要 ATT 许可的跟踪框架。因此，在 Apple 设备上，行为数据收集和相关分析受到限制或不可用。</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>3. 分析工具</h2>
            <p>我们使用 Google Analytics 和 Microsoft Clarity 等分析工具来了解平台使用情况并改进服务。这些工具收集的均为非个人识别数据，例如 IP 地址、大致位置（城市或区域级别）、浏览器类型、会话时长和访问页面。不会与这些服务共享任何可识别个人身份的信息。</p>
            <p><b>注意：</b>在 Apple 设备上，由于 ATT 限制，行为跟踪和跨应用数据收集受到限制。我们完全遵守这些限制，不会绕过，因此来自 Apple 用户的数据可能较少或不存在。</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>4. 数据共享</h2>
            <p>我们不会出售或出租您的个人数据。我们仅与平台核心功能所必需的可信第三方提供商共享数据，例如社交登录提供商、托管服务、分析工具和广告平台。这些提供商均受严格的保密协议约束，且其数据访问权限仅限于必要的信息。</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>5. 数据存储与安全</h2>
            <p>您的数据安全存储在位于美国的 Microsoft Azure 服务器上，并可能在其他地区进行复制以确保稳定性和可用性。数据在传输过程中会加密（如通过 HTTPS），并受到访问控制和监控保护。</p>
            <p>当账户被删除时，个人数据将从主数据库中移除。某些数据可能会在隔离系统中保留长达 6 个月，用于法律或运营原因，例如防止欺诈或符合法规。此后，数据将被永久删除或匿名化。</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>6. 用户权利</h2>
            <p>您可以随时删除账户并请求删除您的数据。您还享有访问、更正或导出数据的权利，可以通过账户设置中的工具或支持渠道实现。</p>
            <p>如果您对数据有疑问，或希望根据适用的隐私法律（GDPR、LGPD、CCPA/CPRA）行使您的权利，请通过平台的支持页面与我们联系。</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>7. 公共和私人清单</h2>
            <p>平台提供由策划的公共清单，任何访问者均可访问和分享。已登录用户可以创建私人清单，项目数量受订阅等级限制。私人清单保持机密，除非用户选择对外分享。</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>8. 儿童和未成年人</h2>
            <p>平台面向普通用户，不会有意收集未达到法定成年年龄儿童的数据。如果我们发现未成年人在未经父母同意的情况下提供了个人信息，我们将采取措施删除该数据。</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>9. 法律合规</h2>
            <p>本政策符合包括 GDPR、LGPD 和 CCPA/CPRA 在内的隐私法律，具体取决于您的所在地。我们会持续审查实践，以确保符合适用法规。</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>10. 联系方式</h2>
            <p>如对您的数据隐私有任何问题、请求或投诉，请使用平台内的支持页面或直接联系我们。</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>11. 本政策的更新</h2>
            <p>我们可能会定期更新本隐私政策，以反映技术、服务或法规的变化。重大变更将在可行时通过通知或电子邮件告知。我们建议您定期查看本政策。</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-footer">
            <p>最后更新日期：2025 年 8 月 5 日</p>
            <p>使用本平台即表示您同意本《隐私政策》和 <a href=@($"/{Culture}/legal/terms")>使用条款</a>。</p>
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        <h1 class="support-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <div class="support-subtitle">
            This Privacy Policy explains how DRMA Tech (Delivering Reliable Modern Apps Tech OÜ), a company registered in Estonia, collects, uses, stores, and shares personal data when you use Streaming Discovery (<a href="@AppInfo.WebSite" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@AppInfo.WebSite</a>), contact us, or use related applications and services.
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
            <p><b>Account information.</b> We process your account identifier, email address, display name, and authentication information. Clerk provides account authentication and identity management.</p>
            <p><b>Saved content and preferences.</b> If you use account features, we store your favorite streaming providers and selected regions, wishlist titles, movies and shows marked as watched, watched episode information, and preferences such as language, region, theme, and platform.</p>
            <p><b>Access and technical information.</b> We may process IP addresses, access dates and times, the country inferred from an IP address, application platform and version, browser and operating system information, page addresses, referrer information, and diagnostic information. Error reports may include stack traces, resource addresses, request metadata, and query parameters relevant to troubleshooting.</p>
            <p><b>Subscription information.</b> We store the payment provider, product, billing cycle, subscription and session identifiers, status, and expiration date. For Apple purchases, the current implementation also stores the purchase receipt submitted for verification.</p>
            <p><b>Feedback and communications.</b> If you submit feedback or contact support, we process the message and information you provide. We also process information needed to send service emails, such as your email address and display name.</p>
            <p>Some discovery features are available without signing in. Account-related features require authentication. Technical information may still be processed when you use the service without an account.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>
            <p>We use information to provide and maintain the service, authenticate users, store preferences and viewing activity, determine approximate country for regional features, manage subscriptions, send service communications, protect the service, detect abuse or fraud, troubleshoot errors, understand usage, improve features, meet legal obligations, and establish or defend legal claims where necessary.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>3. Browser Storage, Cookies, and Similar Technologies</h2>
            <p>The application uses browser local storage and session storage to remember settings and support functionality. Examples include language, region, theme, platform, application version, and session or interface preferences. These mechanisms are not all cookies, but they can store information on your device.</p>
            <p>Third-party services integrated into the application may use cookies, pixels, scripts, or similar technologies. Google AdSense may use cookies or similar identifiers for advertising. Analytics and diagnostic providers may use similar technologies to measure usage and troubleshoot the service.</p>
            <p>The current application does not provide a general in-app cookie or tracking preference center. Browser settings can block or delete some cookies and browser storage, but this may affect functionality and may not prevent all processing by third-party services.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>4. Analytics, Diagnostics, Feedback, and Advertising</h2>
            <p><b>Google Analytics.</b> We use Google Analytics to measure application usage. The integration sends application version and platform information and may process page views, usage events, browser and device information, and IP-derived approximate location.</p>
            <p><b>Microsoft Clarity.</b> We use Clarity to understand how visitors interact with the application. It may collect navigation, clicks or taps, scrolling, and page content needed for session recordings and heatmaps.</p>
            <p><b>Sentry.</b> We use Sentry for error monitoring and diagnostics. Reports may include IP addresses, browser and operating system details, application version, platform, authentication state, page URLs, referrer information, error details, and relevant API request metadata. The browser integration is configured to send default personally identifiable information.</p>
            <p><b>UserJot.</b> We use UserJot for feedback and feature requests. When an authenticated user is identified, we provide the account identifier and email address, together with platform and application version attributes. Feedback submitted through its tools may also be processed by UserJot.</p>
            <p><b>Google AdSense.</b> We use AdSense to display advertisements in eligible placements. Google and its advertising partners may process IP address, browser and device information, cookies or similar identifiers, and advertising interactions to deliver, measure, and protect advertising. Whether advertising is personalized may depend on applicable law and provider settings.</p>
            <p>These tools are initialized automatically in production application contexts in the current implementation. The application currently sends Microsoft Clarity consent values indicating that analytics and advertising storage are granted. The repository does not contain a general consent flow controlling the initialization of all these tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>5. Service Providers and Data Sharing</h2>
            <p>Depending on the feature, relevant information may be disclosed to service providers that operate, secure, support, and improve Streaming Discovery:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Clerk:</b> account authentication and identity management.</li>
                <li><b>Microsoft Azure:</b> application hosting, backend services, and storage of account and application data.</li>
                <li><b>IPinfo:</b> the IP address received by our backend is sent to IPinfo to determine the associated country. The resulting country information is stored in account access records.</li>
                <li><b>Google:</b> analytics and advertising, including Google Analytics and Google AdSense.</li>
                <li><b>Microsoft:</b> Clarity analytics and session interaction analysis.</li>
                <li><b>Sentry:</b> application and backend error monitoring and diagnostics.</li>
                <li><b>UserJot:</b> feedback, feature requests, and authenticated feedback identity.</li>
                <li><b>Stripe:</b> payment processing and subscription management. We send information such as name, email address, account identifier, and subscription details. Payment instrument details are entered with and processed by Stripe.</li>
                <li><b>Apple:</b> in-app purchase and subscription verification. Purchase receipts and transaction identifiers are sent to Apple for verification.</li>
                <li><b>ZeptoMail:</b> service email delivery. We may provide email address, display name, account reference, and information needed to prepare the message. Some update emails may include titles associated with your viewing activity.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>We do not sell personal data for monetary consideration. However, disclosures to analytics and advertising providers may be considered sharing for cross-context behavioral advertising under some privacy laws, including California law. See our <a href=@($"/{Culture}/legal/do-not-sell")>Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information</a> page for related information.</p>
            <p>Providers process information under their own terms and privacy practices and may process it in countries other than your country of residence.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>6. Movie and TV Data Providers</h2>
            <p>Streaming Discovery uses external content services, including TMDB and providers accessed through RapidAPI, to retrieve movie and TV metadata, ratings, news, trailers, and related information. Depending on the feature, our backend may send media identifiers, search parameters, content language, or region-related parameters. These requests are made by our backend and do not include your Streaming Discovery account credentials.</p>
            <p>These providers supply content information and are not used as our account database or payment processors. Their own privacy policies and terms govern their services.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>7. Payments and Subscriptions</h2>
            <p>Subscriptions may be processed by Stripe or Apple, depending on the purchase method available to you. The relevant provider processes the payment and may collect payment details directly from you. Streaming Discovery stores subscription information needed to recognize and manage your plan.</p>
            <p>For Stripe purchases, we store the Stripe customer identifier and subscription or checkout references, together with plan and subscription status information. For Apple purchases, we send the purchase receipt to Apple for verification and store the submitted receipt and transaction identifier in the account subscription record.</p>
            <p>Deleting your Streaming Discovery account does not itself cancel an active subscription. You must cancel it through the relevant provider or platform first. Records held independently by Stripe or Apple are subject to their own privacy policies and retention practices and are not automatically deleted when your Streaming Discovery account is deleted.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>8. Data Storage, Retention, and Account Deletion</h2>
            <p>Account and application data are stored using Microsoft Azure services, including Azure Cosmos DB. We retain account information and saved content while the account remains active or as needed to provide the service, maintain security, resolve disputes, and meet legal obligations.</p>
            <p>Login history is periodically limited to records from the previous six months, with a maximum of 100 recorded accesses. Free accounts may be automatically deleted after at least six months without a recorded access, following an inactivity notification. Accounts with an active subscription are excluded from this inactivity-deletion process.</p>
            <p>You can request account deletion through the Help Center. Account deletion is not available while an active subscription remains on the account. When deletion is completed, our backend deletes the account profile, login history, provider preferences, wishlist, and watching list from the application database and requests deletion of the associated Clerk user.</p>
            <p>Account deletion does not automatically delete records held independently by payment, analytics, advertising, email, or other third-party providers. Those providers may retain information under their own policies and legal obligations. The current application code does not establish a general six-month retention period for all data after account deletion.</p>
            <p>The exact Azure hosting and database regions are determined by deployment configuration. The source code repository does not identify one fixed region for all stored data. Information may be processed in countries outside your country of residence.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>9. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
            <p>Depending on your location and applicable law, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, receive, or transfer your personal data, restrict or object to certain processing, withdraw consent where processing is based on consent, and lodge a complaint with a data protection authority.</p>
            <p>You can download certain information stored by Streaming Discovery using the Download Data action in the Help Center. The export includes application account records, login history, selected providers, wishlist, and watching list. It does not include information held independently by third-party providers.</p>
            <p>To request access, correction, deletion, or exercise another privacy right, contact <a href="mailto:support@streamingdiscovery.com">support@streamingdiscovery.com</a>. We may need to verify your identity before responding. Some information may be retained where required or permitted by law.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>10. Public Information and Shared Content</h2>
            <p>Some curated lists and pages are public and can be viewed by visitors. If you publish or share a list or link, the information made available through that feature may be accessed, copied, or shared by other people. Do not publish or share information that you intend to keep private.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>11. Children and Minors</h2>
            <p>Streaming Discovery is intended for a general audience. If you are below the age of legal majority where you live, you may use the service only with the permission and involvement of a parent or legal guardian where required by law. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children where doing so is prohibited by applicable law. If you believe a child has provided personal information improperly, contact us so we can review the request.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>12. Security</h2>
            <p>We use reasonable technical and organizational measures designed to protect personal data against unauthorized access, loss, misuse, or disclosure. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>13. Changes to This Policy</h2>
            <p>We may update this Privacy Policy to reflect changes to the service, our data practices, our service providers, or applicable law. We will publish the revised version on this page and update the date below. Where required by law, we will provide additional notice or request consent for material changes.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>14. Contact</h2>
            <p>For privacy questions or requests, email <a href="mailto:support@streamingdiscovery.com">support@streamingdiscovery.com</a>. You can also use the <a href=@($"/{Culture}/help")>Help Center</a> for account data and deletion tools. For company or general inquiries, contact <a href="mailto:contact@drma-tech.com">contact@drma-tech.com</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="support-footer">
            <p>Last updated: November 6, 2026</p>
            <p>For information about the service terms, please read our <a href=@($"/{Culture}/legal/terms")>Terms of Use</a>.</p>
        </div>
    }
</div>

